star, my

33
00:03:16,939 --> 00:03:17,769
Shining star, my diamond

34
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,727
man, I got you, so I got you

35
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:09,060
Oh, my God.

36
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:37,940
Who are you?

37
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:39,980
Are you from around here?

38
00:04:40,260 --> 00:04:41,700
Is he a tester like me?

39
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:43,340
Or is he an NPC?

40
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:48,440
Do you have a name?

41
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:52,640
Um, yeah, I got one.

42
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:55,820
It's Kirito.

43
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:58,030
Kirito?

44
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:02,612
I came from the forest over there, But
I'm not sure where I am or anything.

45
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:03,580
The forest.

46
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:05,447
Oh, you mean from the south?

47
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,835
Did you walk all the way from Zakaria?

48
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:09,620
No, I don't think so.

49
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:14,060
I mean, it's like, I
don't know how I got here.

50
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,360
I can't remember. What?

51
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:17,933
Then where do you live?

52
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:19,957
Can you remember the name of the town?

53
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:22,160
Um, no, everything's a blank.

54
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,800
I woke up and I was in the forest.

55
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:29,557
I heard the stories, but I never thought
I'd meet a real life lost child of Vecta.

56
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:30,900
I can't believe it.

57
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:32,470
Huh?

58
00:05:32,553 --> 00:05:33,383
What's a Vecta?

59
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:36,957
Wait, isn't that what they're
called where you're from?

60
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:39,380
When someone disappears from a village,

61
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:43,517
then suddenly turns up in a forest or
a field, that's what they're called,

62
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,700
a child of Vecta.

63
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:47,737
The dark god Vecta likes to prank humans.

64
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:49,055
By snatching them up,

65
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:52,837
stealing their memories, and plopping
them down somewhere far from home.

66
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:57,200
Oh, I guess that must have
been what happened to me then.

67
00:05:59,020 --> 00:06:01,937
His responses are way
too natural for an NPC.

68
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:05,297
I'll try the direct approach anyway.

69
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:07,220
I'm kind of stuck so.

70
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:11,080
I want to leave.

71
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:16,000
Yes, I'm sure you do.

72
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:21,877
I think I know how to help you.

73
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:24,477
The forest is huge and
easy to get lost in though.

74
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:27,000
I can show you a path that leads north.

75
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:28,717
As long as you stick to it, you won't...

76
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:29,630
Sorry.

77
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:31,880
I want to log out now.

78
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:34,140
Log out?

79
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:35,736
What does that mean?

80
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:37,210
Damn it.

81
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,040
It's slang, you know?

82
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:45,500
It's like a faster way of saying I
need to find a place to stay. Really?

83
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:47,525
I never heard that one before.

84
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:50,200
Now what?

85
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:55,080
He could be a tester, but if he is,
his memories are definitely blocked.

86
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:58,617
My village is called Rulid
and it's beyond those trees,

87
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:00,437
but we don't get many travelers,

88
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,579
so there's no win.

89
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:06,037
I think if we go to the church and
explain your situation to Sister Azalea,

90
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:07,885
she might agree to put you up.

91
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,300
Oh, okay then.

92
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:12,033
I'll go to your village and talk to her.

93
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:13,260
Wait a moment.

94
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:17,157
But you're a stranger in these parts.

95
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:21,416
I don't think the guards at the gate
are going to let you in so easily.

96
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:22,910
You know what?

97
00:07:22,993 --> 00:07:25,737
If I go with you and talk to
them, they should understand.

98
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:27,137
That'd be great if you did.

99
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:28,050
Thanks a lot.

100
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:31,117
But I can't go yet.

101
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:33,024
I have to finish my work first.

102
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:36,549
And I won't be done
for another four hours.

103
00:07:37,140 --> 00:07:38,760
I don't mind. I can wait.

104
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:41,277
That is, as long as it's okay with you.

105
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:42,190
Of course.

106
00:07:42,273 --> 00:07:44,917
Have a seat anywhere you
like, and I'll get to work.

107
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,294
Oh, I haven't told you my name, have I?

108
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:48,690
No.

109
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:53,980
My name is Eugeo. How'd you do?

110
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:55,750
Eugeo?

111
00:07:55,833 --> 00:07:56,663
Sounds familiar.

112
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,780
What's wrong, Sir Kirito?

113
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:04,650
Nothing.

114
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:07,600
Oh, and you can just call me Kirito.

115
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,590
Okay.

116
00:08:09,673 --> 00:08:11,534
Nice to make your acquaintance, Kirito.

117
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:15,280
That's right.

118
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:16,710
Huh?

119
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:17,938
You must be hungry.

120
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:20,620
Oh, thanks a lot.

121
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,040
He's definitely not an NPC.

122
00:08:24,780 --> 00:08:27,427
Still not sure if he's
a test player, though.

123
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:30,060
Or maybe this isn't VR.

124
00:08:30,580 --> 00:08:31,980
Maybe this is real.

125
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:36,377
The only good thing about this,
Brett, is it keeps for a long time.

126
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:38,040
But just to be safe.

127
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:45,560
Okay, let me try that.

128
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:49,480
That settles it.

129
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:52,480
This ain't reality or
a parallel dimension.

130
00:08:53,380 --> 00:08:54,400
It's VR.

131
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:56,680
Hey, Kirito. What?

132
00:08:56,900 --> 00:08:59,724
Did you forget how to use
the Stacia window too?

133
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:01,600
No, course not.

134
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:07,877
You can take your time
eating it if you want.

135
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:09,901
It still has plenty of life left.

136
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:14,724
If this were summer, you can bet
it wouldn't keep nearly as long.

137
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:17,790
Huh?

138
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:19,710
Holy!

139
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:23,380
It's not very good, huh?

140
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:26,537
I get them from the bakery
every morning on my way here,

141
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:29,037
but so early they only have day-old bread,

142
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:32,217
and I don't have time to go
back at noon for fresh ones.

143
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:33,130
That sucks.

144
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:36,829
Do you have time to make lunch
or have someone else make it?

145
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:43,241
Well, actually, someone used to bring me
my lunch every day, but that was years ago.

146
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:44,530
Oh, well.

147
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,500
So why'd they stop?

148
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:53,520
She was my childhood friend.

149
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,460
She was the same age as me.

150
00:09:56,980 --> 00:10:00,220
When we were little, we
played together all the time.

151
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:06,000
And after I received my calling, she would
bring me lunch every day without fail.

152
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:08,160
But then,

153
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:15,340
because of me, the two of us went to
explore a cave up north, and by accident,

154
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:18,017
she crossed the boundary
into the Dark Territory,

155
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:20,860
a place no human is
allowed to enter, ever.

156
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:23,380
The Taboo Index forbids it.

157
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:25,040
Taboo Index?

158
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:27,280
The next day,

159
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:29,697
an Integrity Knight came to our village,

160
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:34,640
and he took her to Senator to be executed.

161
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:39,860
But I still believe she's alive, Kirito.

162
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:41,460
I know it.

163
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:45,820
Somewhere in Senator, Alice is alive.

164
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:47,710
Alice.

165
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:49,560
I know that name.

166
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:52,950
Alice.

167
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:55,440
I'm sorry.

168
00:10:56,380 --> 00:10:58,615
I didn't mean to dump all that on you.

169
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:02,565
I know we just met and all, but
it feels like we're old friends.

170
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:04,660
That's okay. I don't mind.

171
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,120
So, why don't you go find her?

172
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:09,908
Go to Senator or wherever.

173
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:11,218
See if she's there.

174
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,680
Even if I had the fastest
horse in the land,

175
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:17,257
it would take a week
to get there from here.

176
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:20,340
Then throw some clothes
and food in a bag and walk.

177
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:23,037
If I could do that, I would.

178
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:25,540
But I can't just abandon my calling.

179
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:27,660
The Taboo Index forbids it.

180
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:28,780
You know that.

181
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:31,600
Oh, right. You got a point.

182
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:38,540
Um, sorry to be nosy, but about how
long ago did all this happen anyway?

183
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:42,060
It was my 11th summer, six years ago.

184
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:44,121
Want some water?

185
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:48,956
Thanks, maybe later.

186
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:52,777
Well, lunch is over, so I
better get back to work.

187
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:54,877
I still have to meet my quota for today.

188
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:57,372
I'll just kick back till you finish then.

189
00:11:57,460 --> 00:11:59,797
By the way, you're calling. What is it?

190
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:00,840
You'll see.

191
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:02,540
It's not very exciting.

192
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:28,605
So, like, you're calling
us to chop down trees?

193
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:30,510
Yeah.

194
00:12:30,593 --> 00:12:32,417
Officially, my title's
supposed to be woodcutter.

195
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:34,937
The problem is I haven't
cut a single tree down

196
00:12:35,020 --> 00:12:37,577
in the seven years since
I received my calling.

197
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:38,490
What?

198
00:12:38,573 --> 00:12:40,085
My job's to work on this tree.

199
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:41,780
It's called the Giga Cedar.

200
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:44,757
The villagers call it
something else, though.

201
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:46,140
The Demon Tree.

202
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:49,377
They call it that because
it sucks up all of

203
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:52,107
Terraria's blessings
from the land around it.

204
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:54,897
Rulid has always wanted to
plant more wheat fields,

205
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:58,039
but as long as this is here,
nothing good will grow.

206
00:12:58,160 --> 00:13:01,017
The village had that dragon bone
axe sent from the capital and

207
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:05,017
appointed a woodcutter to work on it
every day till the tree came down.

208
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:06,100
That's my job.

209
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:10,680
So, for the past seven years now,
you've been chopping away at it?

210
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:15,520
After all that time, that's
as far as you got? Hardly.

211
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:19,287
I'm actually a seventh
generation woodcutter.

212
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:20,918
That's our calling.

213
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:22,537
Someone's been chopping away on it.

214
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:23,720
Every single day.

215
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,480
For 300 years, in fact.

216
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:27,480
For 300 years?

217
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:33,420
Hey, Yu-Gi-Oh.

218
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:37,040
Mind if I take a crack at it? Huh?

219
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:41,119
I mean, you did give me
half your lunch, didn't you?

220
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:44,177
So it's only fair I should
pick up half your work.

221
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:45,540
Oh, I don't know.

222
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:48,917
I mean, the taboo index doesn't
say I can't have someone help,

223
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,176
even though it is my calling and all.

224
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:53,957
Try it, but it's much
harder than it looks.

225
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:55,940
I won't know till I try.

226
00:13:56,620 --> 00:13:57,760
Here goes nothing.

227
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,500
You don't have to laugh that hard.

228
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:23,080
I'm sorry about that.

229
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:27,377
You put way too much tension
into your shoulders and hips.

230
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:30,225
Relax and let the momentum
do the work for you.

231
00:14:32,820 --> 00:14:33,740
That's right.

232
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:35,720
This is a virtual world.

233
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,140
It's not about my real
ability, but my avatars.

234
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,020
Sword skill?

235
00:14:47,580 --> 00:14:48,410
Smash!

236
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:02,220
Whoa, that was a nice hit.

237
00:15:02,580 --> 00:15:06,100
Go on, give it another
shot before you forget.

238
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:08,370
Fifty!

239
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,420
Okay, that's one thousand strikes.

240
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:15,530
Really?

241
00:15:15,613 --> 00:15:16,720
We did that many today?

242
00:15:17,780 --> 00:15:18,610
Uh-huh.

243
00:15:18,693 --> 00:15:20,397
Five hundred for me and
five hundred for you.

244
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:24,337
At the thousand I did this morning,
and that's 2,000 strikes total.

245
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:26,655
That's the daily quota for my calling.

246
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:28,660
Oh, my God.

247
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:31,197
You're a natural at this, Kirito.

248
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:33,986
Thanks to your skill, I
had an easy day today.

249
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:35,492
I don't know about that.

250
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:40,651
I bet you would have had it cut down
by now if I wasn't here messing around.

251
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:43,130
Think so?

252
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:45,064
Then you need to see something.

253
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:52,417
It's only gone down by about 50 since
last month that's normal actually

254
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:57,357
it's a strong tree so what if we
didn't make a lot of progress today in

255
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,117
the end it doesn't really make much

256
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:05,797
of a difference at all let's go wait

257
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:10,777
you forgot to lock it what for what
do you mean someone could steal it?

258
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:12,420
Now who'd do that?

259
00:16:12,620 --> 00:16:16,517
It clearly states in the taboo index
that theft is forbidden, remember?

260
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,020
Oh, yeah, that's right.

261
00:16:18,500 --> 00:16:20,500
Come on, I'll show you my village.

262
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,740
Um, but...

263
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:24,500
Hey, wait up!

264
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:43,560
Hey, Eugeo.

265
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:46,554
Who's your new friend?

266
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:48,750
Hey, Zink.

267
00:16:48,833 --> 00:16:49,980
This is Kirito.

268
00:16:50,940 --> 00:16:53,560
I think he's a lost child of Vecta.

269
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:55,480
That true?

270
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:57,327
You can't remember anything?

271
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:58,740
Um, no.

272
00:16:59,180 --> 00:17:01,057
Did you forget your calling, too?

273
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:02,140
Yeah, I guess.

274
00:17:03,340 --> 00:17:05,760
It was probably a lousy calling anyway.

275
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:09,280
Bet it was as lame as Eugeo's here.

276
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:13,429
He's got one of the most pointless
callings in all the land.

277
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:17,117
Now mine, I'm a man-at-arms,
and let me tell...

278
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,030
Swordsman.

279
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:19,993
That's my calling, man.

280
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:21,500
I'm a swordsman.

281
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:23,100
A swordsman?

282
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:25,920
A scrawny, weak-looking
pipsqueak like you?

283
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:27,747
You can't even lift a sword.

284
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:33,020
Go on, then.

285
00:17:33,300 --> 00:17:34,880
Show us your skill.

286
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,960
Let's see how I do with this.

287
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:02,560
No way.

288
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:07,200
That was a light effect.

289
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:09,780
There's sword skills here.

290
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,920
That was amazing.

291
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:14,974
I didn't know you had skills like that.

292
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:18,000
Maybe you were a sentinel
in some big city.

293
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:19,860
I don't know. Maybe.

294
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:23,400
Zink, will you let Kirito in?

295
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:26,188
I'd like to show him
around the village now.

296
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:36,660
I'm tired.

297
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:39,400
Well, we're here. Finally.

298
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:41,940
Is this really okay?

299
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:46,397
I mean, everyone's just going to accept
I'm one of those lost Vecta kids?

300
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:47,892
Isn't that what you are?

301
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:50,320
Yeah, I guess so.

302
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:54,064
Let's talk to the sister
and get you sorted out.

303
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,120
What do you boys want?

304
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:17,371
Here, I brought you a pillow and a blanket

305
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:20,486
Prayers begin at 6 o
'clock, breakfast is at 7

306
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:26,140
I'll come check on you, but please try to
get up on time Do not be late for prayers

307
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:30,080
You do not want to make
Sister Azalea mad Also,

308
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:33,025
we have a curfew after
life's out, so mind that

309
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:34,260
Jesus! Run!

310
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:37,330
Honestly.

311
00:19:37,413 --> 00:19:39,097
Now then, do you have any questions?

312
00:19:39,180 --> 00:19:40,180
No, I'm good.

313
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:42,091
Thanks for setting me up.

314
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:45,073
Well, good night, then.

315
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:47,853
You know how to put out the lamp, right?

316
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:49,570
Yeah.

317
00:19:49,653 --> 00:19:50,483
Good night, Selka.

318
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:09,160
This ain't the real world and as far as I
can tell none of the villagers are NPCs.

319
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:12,457
But they can't be testers
either there'd have

320
00:20:12,540 --> 00:20:14,917
to be dozens of STLs
for them to log in with.

321
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
and I know there aren't that many.

322
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:19,340
What did Yu-Gi-Oh say?

323
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:26,485
According to him, more than 300
years have passed in this world.

324
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:31,660
He spent the last six as a woodcutter
here and remembers his childhood here too.

325
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:36,380
If that's true, then him and the others...

326
00:20:40,220 --> 00:20:41,050
Hmm?

327
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:44,110
Oh.

328
00:20:49,420 --> 00:20:52,437
Yu-Gi-Oh and the villagers were
raised here from the start,

329
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:57,660
but the only way that could happen is
if Wrath copied the souls of babies.

330
00:20:58,960 --> 00:20:59,790
Babies.

331
00:21:01,020 --> 00:21:02,373
Artificial Fluctlights.

332
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:05,817
It's hard to believe, but
there's no other explanation.

333
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:07,980
But why would Wrath do that?

334
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:12,846
And how fast would they have to accelerate
time to get this world to this point?

335
00:21:15,360 --> 00:21:19,300
And what if I'm stuck here
forever and never get back home?

336
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:25,760
Maybe I can get in touch with Kikuoka
if I can get to a bigger city.

337
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:29,200
I need money to travel
and right now I got none.

338
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:32,227
And I don't know enough
about this world yet.

339
00:21:34,580 --> 00:21:40,740
If I had some help, I could get to
Senator and find some answers there.

340
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:48,897
I'm proud of you,

341
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:55,557
and I'm proud of you,

342
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:58,920
and I'm proud of you.

343
00:22:28,980 --> 00:22:31,580
I'll see you soon.

344
00:23:12,840 --> 00:23:14,899
If you feel that you're next to me,

345
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:20,680
I've been hiding that hurt.

346
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:25,880
I'll have to heal that hurt a little bit.

347
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:28,820
Realist to you.
